      "title": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland",
      "gist": "Modern work lets people earn impersonal respect and dignity independent of family or clan, a freedom that purely relational societies struggle to provide.",
      "question": "friendship and commerce — why does paid work make modern friendship freer than relationships in purely relational societies? (historical argument)",
      "sourceHeading": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland"
    },
